package-lock.json
# pnpm-lock.yaml is COMMITTED on purpose — this tier is a GATE. It used to be
# ignored, which meant a fresh worktree re-resolved `^1.59.1` and could pull a
# playwright whose Chromium build is not in the local cache: that turned the
# whole 39-file sweep into spurious FAILs (observed 2026-07-26, 1.62.0 vs the
# 1.61.0 every other tree had). Specifiers in package.json are EXACT and this
# lockfile is the reproducibility contract — install with --frozen-lockfile.
